    921  f0ff							; for a blank line at band boundaries — shipped pre-99b8e86 without
    922  f0ff							; either; case15 filters zero writes so the Y-align guard is unaffected.
    923  f0ff							; --- Scanlines this pass (N=4): bands 0-2 = 36; band 3 = 24+off (tide,
    924  f0ff							; CollisionX). The bottom water strip (last 12-off lines,
    925  f0ff							; bottom_band_plan rule 2) renders in .WaterRow after this pass — its own
    926  f0ff							; setup line + (12-off) bodies, so the bottom band spans 38 picture lines
    927  f0ff							; and the cave body count is exactly CAVE_LINES (144).
    928  f0ff							; Split tail (2026-10-05, row1 setup gap 77->74): the non-bottom gate used
    929  f0ff							; to pay `bne` 3c to skip the tide load AND share the WSYNC — gap was 77
    930  f0ff							; (stall, +1 line/frame). Non-bottom bands now store+WSYNC before the tide
    931  f0ff							; block, then jmp over it (+3c charged to the FIRST body line =
    932  f0ff							; 66max+3jmp+3WSYNC = 72 <=76). Bottom-band path byte-identical in cost
    933  f0ff							; (cpx/beqT/lda/sta/WSYNC
    934  f0ff							; = 11+3 = 76, zero margin — the `beq` target is 9 bytes ahead, same
    935  f0ff							; page, T=3c; do not let this block grow toward a page edge).
    936  f0ff							; A1 gap fix (2026-10-05): `sta Temp` (+3c in .Row) pushed gaps to
    937  f0ff							; 77/79 = stall EVERY frame (265-line frames). `sta LineCount` moved
    938  f0ff							; AFTER `sta WSYNC` — same bytes, -3c from the gap window, +3c to the
    939  f0ff							; first body line (66max+3LC[+3jmp]+3WSYNC = 75 rows0/1, 72 row2).
    940  f0ff							; LineCount is not read until the line's `dec` tail — the early store
    941  f0ff							; was never required; keep the store strictly between WSYNC and .Line.
